{"issue_id": "TRACK_M_CURRENT_BAR_FILTER", "status": "false_alarm", "severity": "high", "first_flagged": "2026-10-05", "report_date": "2026-10-05", "exact_line": "| EXECUTION BUG | HIGH | `day_tier_track_m.py` | Friday Close Fetch | `fetch_bars_window` windowing includes the current Monday bar; the `_dates` filter is insufficient if Alpaca provides a 00:00:00 timestamped bar for the current day, causing `last.date() != prev_session`. |", "match_keywords": [], "notes": "Verified 2026-10-07: Track M converts every daily timestamp to ET and filters x < now_et.date() before selecting the final bar. tests/test_day_tier_track_m.py::Evaluate::test_todays_forming_daily_bar_is_ignored supplies a Monday forming bar and proves Friday is used."}
{"issue_id": "DAY_TIER_MAINTENANCE_RATE_INVERSION", "status": "false_alarm", "severity": "medium", "first_flagged": "2026-10-05", "report_date": "2026-10-05", "exact_line": "| ALPHA ISSUE | MEDIUM | `day_tier_manager.py` | `_bounded_entry_qty` | The `maintenance` room calculation uses `maintenance_rate`. If `maintenance_rate` is 1.0 (standard for some paper assets), but the broker requires 100% for volatile stocks (e.g., MSTR, MARA), the cushion check will under-estimate required margin. |", "match_keywords": [], "notes": "Verified 2026-10-07: the broker returns the asset-specific maintenance_margin_requirement as a fraction. A rate of 1.0 means 100% maintenance and is the strictest accepted value; dividing available equity by 1.0 cannot under-estimate a requirement above 100%."}
